# 📘 Data Engineer Interview Preparation – Follow-up Questions

This document contains commonly asked follow-up questions based on my self-introduction for Data Engineer interviews, along with structured answers.
---------------------------------------------------------------------
## 🔹 1. Explain your current project in detail

It’s a batch ETL pipeline where data is ingested from source systems into Amazon S3. Then we process it using PySpark on AWS EMR or AWS Glue.
We perform data cleaning, validation, and transformations, and then store processed data for querying using Amazon Athena.
I mainly handle monitoring, validation, failure handling, and reconciliation to ensure data accuracy.

Sample Syntax:

df = spark.read.csv("s3://bucket/input")
df_clean = df.filter(df["col"].isNotNull())
df_clean.write.mode("overwrite").parquet("s3://bucket/output")
--------------------------------------------------------------------

## 🔹 2. What exactly is your role?

I monitor data loads, validate data quality, handle failures, and perform reconciliation. I also work on PySpark transformations and support optimization of pipelines when performance issues occur.

Sample Validation Syntax:

source_count = df_source.count()
