## 🔹 3. How do you handle data failures?

First, I identify the failure by checking logs. Then I analyze the root cause — whether it’s a data issue, schema mismatch, or resource issue. Finally, I fix the issue and rerun the job, ensuring data consistency.
---------------------------------------------------------------------

## 🔹 4. Explain incremental load

Incremental load means processing only new or updated data instead of the entire dataset. I implement it using timestamps or last processed values, filtering only new records and appending them to the target.

Sample Syntax:

df_new = df.filter(df["updated_date"] > last_processed_date)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

